      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "FIGO (2) sets the standard after consecutive Mdn seconds, the latest at Emerald when beaten a length and a half despite jumping awkwardly, racing wide near the 900m and laying out in the straight. He has placed in two of three tries around 1000m and looks ready third-up. WILLBEKING (4) is the durable danger, placed at Charleville and St George and with enough 1000m consistency to keep pressure on, although being beaten as favourite last start tempers the enthusiasm slightly. EARLY EDITION (1) was bumped early when fourth to Eminen at Emerald and rates well, but he must overturn the FIGO form and his 1000m record is plain. OUR LAST CHANCE (9) improved into second at Twin Hills and gets here fourth-up, yet she is another with an unconvincing record around this trip, so her best case is building on that latest placing. BELLAH'S HOPE (5) finished third last start, beaten 1.5 lengths at Thangool over 800m. Watch for market value.",
